  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry weather prevails for the rest of this week\nwith moderating temperatures. Next rain chance late in the \nweekend into early next week.\n\nHigh pressure will continue to dominate the weather throughout\nthis week featuring clear skies, cool overnights and warm\ndaytime highs. \n\nTemperatures should moderate somewhat as the center of high \npressure reaches the East Coast mid-week. The flow will turn \ntowards the southwest during Wednesday and Thursday to boost \ntemperatures into the 70s and 80s. A dry frontal passage to the\nnorth late Thursday could bring slightly cooler air by Friday, \nbut another area of high pressure should keep conditions dry \nthrough Saturday. The lack of rainfall this week will only \nworsen the ongoing drought across the Piedmont. \n\nNext rainfall chance comes late in the weekend and into early\nnext week with a potential for a tropical system forming in\nGulf, then moving north across the southeast United States.\nHowever, this system has still not developed in the Gulf, so \nthis portion of the forecast remains very low confidence.",
